Package: amule
Architecture: any
Depends: amule-common (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
Recommends: amule-utils,
Suggests: amule-utils-gui,
Description: client for the eD2k and Kad networks, like eMule
 aMule is a peer-to-peer file sharing application for the eDonkey and Kad
 networks. It has most features of eMule, including source exchange,
 compressed transfers, secure identification, IP filtering, and searches
 on servers and in the Kad network.
 .
 The amule-daemon package has a version that runs without a graphical
 session. The amule-utils and amule-utils-gui packages have related
 utilities, including the ed2k link handler.

Package: amule-common
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
Recommends: wx3.2-i18n,
Description: common files for the aMule packages
 This package contains the files that the other aMule packages share:
 translations, GUI skins, icons, desktop integration for eMule
 collection files, the media metadata helper, and a private copy of
 the wxWidgets libraries. Install amule, amule-daemon, amule-utils or
 amule-utils-gui instead of this package alone.

Package: amule-daemon
Architecture: any
Depends: amule-common (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
Recommends: amule-utils,
Description: aMule daemon and REST API, for the eD2k and Kad networks
 This package contains amuled, a version of aMule that does not need a
 graphical session. It is normally used on a machine that runs 24/7.
 .
 It also contains amuleapi, a REST API server with a web interface that
 controls amuled or amule. amulecmd (in amule-utils) and amulegui (in
 amule-utils-gui) can also control the daemon.

Package: amule-utils
Architecture: any
Depends: amule-common (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
Description: command-line utilities for aMule
 This package contains command-line utilities for aMule:
 .
  * ed2k: sends ed2k:// links to aMule
  * cas: shows the contents of your aMule online signature
  * alcc: makes ed2k:// links for the given files
  * amulecmd: text client that controls aMule or the aMule daemon
 .
 The amule-utils-gui package has graphical versions of some of them.

Package: amule-utils-gui
Architecture: any
Depends: amule-common (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
Description: graphical utilities for aMule
 This package contains graphical utilities for aMule:
 .
  * amulegui: graphical client that controls aMule or the aMule daemon
  * wxcas: shows the contents of your aMule online signature
  * alc: makes ed2k:// links for the given files
 .
 The amule-utils package has command-line versions of them.
